{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-015-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/MapRender/CutoverHardeningTests.cs","line":414,"method":"SpineFallbackWarnedPidSet_IsClearedOnReset","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/MapRender/ShadowRenderDriver.cs:118; delete spineFallbackWarnedPids.Clear() from Reset() -> still green; seeding a pid through a new test seam first -> red","what_it_asserts":"that SpineFallbackWarnedPidCountForTesting is 0 immediately after ShadowRenderDriver.Reset()","why_weak":"the set is empty for the whole headless lifetime (its only writer, the private WarnSpineAssemblerFallback, is unreachable from xUnit), so the assertion is 0 == 0 and a Reset that stopped clearing (silencing the C4 one-shot warn forever after the first scene) leaves it green","proposed_action":"add an internal MarkSpineFallbackWarnedForTesting(pid) seam (or make WarnSpineAssemblerFallback internal), seed one pid, assert the count is 1, Reset, assert 0","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-015-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/MapRender/CutoverHardeningTests.cs","line":427,"method":"RunFrame_ColdLoadGuard_DoesNotPruneStaleState_SourceGate","category":"T4","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/MapRender/ShadowRenderDriver.cs:322; change the VerboseRateLimited window 5.0 -> 10.0 -> red with no behavior change; insert PruneStaleState(); at line 326 -> red","what_it_asserts":"that the raw source contains the comment 'PruneStaleState is intentionally NOT called' and that the comment-stripped, whitespace-collapsed source contains the literal '5.0); return; }'","why_weak":"one half reads a COMMENT as the contract (the rubric's comments-read-as-code trap), the other couples the gate to an unrelated rate-limit constant and to statement ordering, so it reds on innocent edits and passes if the comment survives a real prune","proposed_action":"replace both with a scoped check that the defer block (from 'if (!IsLiveClockReady(currentUT))' to its closing brace) contains no 'PruneStaleState' call, extracted by brace matching as the sibling terrain gates do","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-015-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/Rendering/FlightRecorderTerrainTests.cs","line":213,"method":"RecordedClearance_EqualsAltitudeMinusTerrain","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/ParsekFlight.cs ResolvePhase7EffectiveAltitude; return recordedAltitude on the finite-clearance path -> red on the round-trip assert; no recorder-side change can red this test","what_it_asserts":"that altitude - terrainHeight equals the InlineData expectedClearance (test-side arithmetic), then that the render helper round-trips altitude when play-time terrain equals recording-time terrain","why_weak":"the name and comment claim the RECORDER clearance contract, but no recorder code is exercised; the first assertion is a tautology over constants and only the round-trip half can fail","proposed_action":"drop the inline-arithmetic assertion and rename to state the render round-trip, or call the recorder-side clearance computation directly if it is reachable headlessly","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
